course: dictionary
lesson: 14930
title: Regardless
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Regardless is a word for carrying on even when something could stop you. It means without paying attention to problems, warnings or difficulties; anyway. «The rain was heavy, but the team played on regardless.» The rain was a problem, and the team did not let it stop them.
explain: Regardless of is a phrase with a second meaning: not being affected by something. «Everyone is welcome regardless of age.» Age does not decide whether you can come. To check, swap in «no matter» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Look at the words around regardless to decide which meaning fits. If someone keeps going despite danger or warnings, it means anyway. If something does not change because of a factor, it means regardless of that factor. The spelling is regard-less, with no «i».
fact: Regardless means anyway, without paying attention to problems, warnings or difficulties.
fact: «Regardless of» means without being affected by something.
fact: «Everyone is welcome regardless of age» means age does not stop anyone from coming.
fact: Two phrases to know are «regardless of» and «carry on regardless».
fact: In stories, a character may carry on regardless of danger.
exercise: «The storm was getting worse, but the sailors sailed on regardless.» What does regardless mean here? | Quickly and quietly | Only if the sea was calm | *Anyway, without paying attention to the storm | Because the storm had stopped
exercise: «The club is open to everyone regardless of their height.» What does regardless of mean here? | Because everyone is tall | Only for tall people | *Without being affected by how tall someone is | Only if they are small
exercise: Ella's mum says, «Do the maths test regardless of the weather.» What does this suggest? | The test is cancelled if it rains | You must wait until the weather is sunny | *The weather does not change whether you do the test | You do the test only in summer
test: «Despite the warnings, Max rode his bike down the icy hill regardless.» What does regardless mean? | *Anyway, ignoring the warnings | Slowly and carefully | Only when it was dry | Because the warnings told him to
test: Choose the best word: The prize goes to every child ___ their age. | in spite of | because of | *regardless of | after
exam: The coach shouted, «Play on regardless!» What does regardless mean? | Stop and go home | Only if you feel like it | Quietly, so no one can hear | *Keep going, without stopping for problems
